      "claim": "(S)-Methadone has an absolute oral bioavailability of 0.88 ± 0.12 in human subjects, supporting high F.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C08"],
      "claim": "Even fexofenadine, a piperidine-containing zwitterion with P-gp liability, has absolute oral bioavailability around 30%, above the 20% threshold, supporting high F.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C30"],
      "claim": "Levomethadone has approximately 75% oral bioavailability in humans, supporting high F.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C50"],
      "claim": "A phenyl/pyridyl dimethylamino analogue (DMD) has 50% oral bioavailability in normal subjects, supporting high F.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C47"],
      "claim": "Bepotastine, a pyridyl piperidine analogue, has >80% oral bioavailability in humans, supporting high F.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C25"],
      "claim": "Desethyloxybutynin enantiomers have 62–78% oral bioavailability in healthy adults, supporting high F.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C05"],
      "claim": "Loperamide is a low-F (0.3%) piperidine analogue, but its very low transfer score and distinct amide/chlorophenyl/P-gp liabilities make it a weak contradictory outlier.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "The query is a 2,6-dimethylpiperidine analogue of the disopyramide/methadone family, with a phenyl/pyridyl carbinol and basic amine. Multiple high-transfer human absolute bioavailability measurements for close analogues (disopyramide 75–90%, methadone 70–90%, dextromoramide good, bepotastine >80%) consistently support F >=20%. The only low-F analogue, loperamide, has very low transferability and distinct P-gp/amide liabilities. Therefore predict high.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct experimental bioavailability data for the query molecule.",
    "The high basic pKa (10.35) and full ionization at pH 7.4 could affect permeability, but similar ionizable basic amines in disopyramide and methadone still show high F.",
    "No data on P-gp efflux or first-pass metabolism for the query."
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [],
  "revision_action": "initial"
}

